    "rationale": "Activating GUCY2C variants increase guanylate cyclase C signaling and intracellular cGMP. Elevated cGMP can hyperactivate CFTR-dependent chloride secretion, driving luminal water secretion and autosomal-dominant familial diarrhea. Strongest alternative resolved: Reduced sodium-glucose cotransport can produce osmotic diarrhea, but it does not follow from an activating GUCY2C receptor variant. The demonstrated pathway is excess GC-C signaling, increased intracellular cGMP, and enhanced chloride/water secretion."
